{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>Please do not leave.</b> נָא is nothing but a term of request — lest they say: Jethro did not convert out of love; he thought converts had a portion in the land. Now that he saw they have no portion, he left them and went his way (there)." "<b>For therefore you know our encampments in the wilderness.</b> For it is fitting for you to do this, because you know our encampments in the wilderness and saw the miracles and mighty acts done for us." "<b>For therefore you know.</b> Like 'because you know' — as in ״כִּי עַל כֵּן לֹא נְתַתִּיהָ לְשֵׁלָה בְּנִי״ (Genesis 38), ״כִּי עַל כֵּן עֲבַרְתֶּם״ (Genesis 19), ״כִּי עַל כֵּן בָּאוּ״ (Genesis 19), ״כִּי עַל כֵּן רָאִיתִי פָנֶיךָ״ (Genesis 33)." "<b>And you have been to us for eyes.</b> Past tense, as its Targum renders. Another interpretation: future tense — every matter hidden from our eyes, you will enlighten our eyes. Another interpretation: that you be dear to us as the pupil of our eye, as it says (Deuteronomy 10) ״וַאֲהַבְתֶּם אֶת הַגֵּר״ (Sifrei)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:15.938954123Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}